# Cloudflare redirects (Workers Static Assets honours the Pages format)
# Format: <source> <destination> <status>
#
# This file is the SINGLE source of truth for download URLs.
# The HTML never links to GitHub directly. When a new version ships, nothing
# here changes — the GitHub "latest" alias and the version-less asset names
# (electron/package.json artifactName) keep every URL below stable.

# === Direct downloads (site buttons without a campaign) ===
/download/win   https://github.com/Freelance-Easy/InvoiceGenerator-releases/releases/latest/download/Freelance-Easy-Setup.exe   302
/download/mac   https://github.com/Freelance-Easy/InvoiceGenerator-releases/releases/latest/download/Freelance-Easy.dmg         302

# === Campaign download paths ===
# Ads and campaign pages link to /dl/<os>/<campaign> so a download click can be
# attributed to a campaign without query strings and without any tracking
# pixel. The trailing splat is the campaign label: a flight's label from the
# allowlist in script.js (CAMPAIGNS, e.g. /dl/mac/f1) or the page's own
# (/dl/mac/mac). Same files as above; the file name never carries the label.
# These redirects do NOT drop a query string: Cloudflare passes it on to
# GitHub (seen 2026-10-04: /dl/mac/f1?probe=1 -> ...Freelance-Easy.dmg?probe=1).
# So never link a /dl/ path with one. The site's buttons never add one, and
# GitHub sees only our origin as the referrer (Referrer-Policy in _headers).
/dl/mac/*   https://github.com/Freelance-Easy/InvoiceGenerator-releases/releases/latest/download/Freelance-Easy.dmg         302
/dl/win/*   https://github.com/Freelance-Easy/InvoiceGenerator-releases/releases/latest/download/Freelance-Easy-Setup.exe   302

# === General ===
/download       https://github.com/Freelance-Easy/InvoiceGenerator-releases/releases   302
/releases       https://github.com/Freelance-Easy/InvoiceGenerator-releases/releases   302

# Pretty URLs (Cloudflare serves /privacy.html for /privacy automatically;
# these catch the trailing-slash variants).
/privacy/     /privacy     301
/terms/       /terms       301
/mac-audio/   /mac-audio   301
/audio/       /audio       301
